# Project Data Dictionary and Metric Definitions

This document describes the workbook created by the notebook and the safest interpretation of its measures. The row-level `Scored_Customers` sheet is the primary customer table. `Model_Comparison` and `Threshold_Analysis` contain test-set evaluation summaries and should remain separate from the full-customer scoring table.

## Workbook sheets

| Sheet | Grain | Use |
|---|---|---|
| `Scored_Customers` | One row per customer | Customer filters, descriptive churn analysis, risk segmentation, and score review |
| `KPI_Summary` | One row for the full file | Reconciliation reference; recreate measures from `Scored_Customers` for filter-responsive cards |
| `Segment_Summary` | One row per Contract × InternetService combination | Reconciliation/reference summary; prefer dynamic measures from `Scored_Customers` for slicer-responsive visuals |
| `Model_Comparison` | One row per candidate model | Compare held-out test-set metrics |
| `Threshold_Analysis` | One row per probability threshold | Show held-out test-set precision, recall, F1, and workload trade-offs |
| `Risk_Summary` | One row per operational risk tier | Reconcile tier counts, observed churn, scores, and monthly charges |
| `Reconciliation_Log` | One row per quality check | Verify record counts, null checks, and key totals |

## `Scored_Customers` fields

| Field | Meaning | Use / caution |
|---|---|---|
| `customerID` | Customer identifier | Count distinct IDs; do not use as a predictor or chart category |
| `gender`, `SeniorCitizen`, `Partner`, `Dependents` | Demographic/account profile fields | Use only for descriptive breakdowns relevant to the project; avoid implying causation |
| `tenure` | Customer tenure in months | Numeric value; useful for lifecycle analysis |
| `TenureGroup` | Bands: 0–6, 7–12, 13–24, 25–48, 49–72 months | Use for readable churn-rate charts; keep categories in this natural order |
| `Contract` | Month-to-month, one-year, or two-year contract | Key descriptive segment |
| `InternetService` | DSL, fiber optic, or no internet service | Key descriptive segment |
| `PaymentMethod` | Customer payment method | Electronic check has the highest observed churn rate in this dataset |
| `PaperlessBilling` | Whether paperless billing is enabled | Descriptive attribute only |
| `NumAddonServices` | Count of selected add-on services marked Yes | Derived feature; includes OnlineSecurity, OnlineBackup, DeviceProtection, TechSupport, StreamingTV, and StreamingMovies |
| `MonthlyCharges` | Monthly charge in the source data | A recurring-charge measure; total by high-risk group is a monthly-charge proxy, not expected loss |
| `TotalCharges` | Accumulated charges, converted to numeric | Highly related to tenure; do not interpret its model effect independently without care |
| `AvgMonthlySpend` | `TotalCharges / tenure`, with current monthly charge used at zero tenure | Derived field close to `MonthlyCharges`; ablation results show only small changes on this split |
| `Churn` | Historical outcome, Yes or No | Actual observed outcome, not a prediction |
| `ChurnFlag` | 1 if `Churn` is Yes, else 0 | Binary version of historical outcome; mean equals actual churn rate |
| `ChurnProbability` | Selected model's estimated score for a customer | Continuous score; calibration needs separate assessment, especially after SMOTE |
| `PredictedChurnFlag50` | 1 when `ChurnProbability >= 0.50` | Model classification at 50%; threshold-dependent |
| `PredictedChurnFlag60` | 1 when `ChurnProbability >= 0.60` | Threshold flag; aligns with High tier when tier boundaries are applied as documented |
| `RiskTier` | Low below 30%; Medium 30% to under 60%; High 60% or above | Operational reporting bands, not validated action rules |

## Core measures

| Measure | Definition | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| Actual churn rate | Churned customers ÷ customers in current filter context | Historical share that churned |
| Average predicted probability | Average of `ChurnProbability` in current filter context | Mean model score for these records; not the historical churn rate |
| Predicted churn rate @ 50% | Share with `PredictedChurnFlag50 = 1` | Model-flagged share at the 50% threshold |
| Predicted churn rate @ 60% | Share with `PredictedChurnFlag60 = 1` | Model-flagged share at the 60% threshold |
| High-risk rate | Share with `RiskTier = High` | High operational-tier share; should match the 60% threshold share if bins and flag are consistent |
| High-risk monthly charges | Sum of `MonthlyCharges` for High-tier customers | Monthly charges associated with high-risk records; not forecast revenue loss or expected customer lifetime value |
| Precision | True positive predictions ÷ all positive predictions | Share of flagged customers who actually churned, evaluated on the test set |
| Recall | True positive predictions ÷ all actual churners | Share of test-set churners detected |
| F1 | Harmonic mean of precision and recall | Single summary of the precision/recall balance |
| AUC | Area under ROC curve | Ranking discrimination across thresholds; not calibration |
| Brier score | Mean squared difference between predicted probabilities and outcomes | Lower is better for probability error, but alone does not prove calibration |

## Evaluation versus scoring

The model-comparison and threshold sheets are derived from the **1,409-row untouched test set**. The `Scored_Customers` sheet contains all **7,043** customers, including training records. Keep these grains visibly separate in Power BI: use the test-set sheets to discuss model performance, and the full-customer sheet for historical segmentation and scoring.

